#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# logical_expand

#% text
# `logical_expand(e)` writes the Boolean combination `e` as a sum of products by distributing `and` over `or`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# An equation whose left side is a series at 0 gives the conjunction of the equations of its coefficients up to the order.

#% item
# `implies`, `equivalent`, `xor`, `nand` and `nor` are replaced by `and`, `or` and `not`, and negations are pushed to the atoms.

#% item
# Any other subexpression (an equation, a comparison, a call) is an atom.

#% item
# Repeated factors and terms that are contradictory or contain another term are dropped; `boolean_convert` finds a smaller form.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
logical_expand((a or b) and (a or c))
#% output
#= a or b and c

#% cell
logical_expand(xor(a, b))
#% output
#= a and not b or not a and b

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Equations as atoms:

#% cell
logical_expand((x == 1 or x == 2) and (y == 3 or y == 4))
#% output
#= x == 1 and y == 3 or x == 1 and y == 4 or x == 2 and y == 3 or x == 2 and y == 4

#% cell
logical_expand(not (a and (b or c)))
#% output
#= not a or not b and not c

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `boolean_convert`, `boolean_minimize`
